															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/silberescher" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(304355); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=304355&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606467121" alt="Silberescher" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=304355)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/silberescher" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(304355); return false;" >Silberescher</a></span> <span class="odate time_1391724348 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Feb 2014 22:05</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1959003">
									

<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Show&nbsp;Rambling</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Hide&nbsp;Rambling</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This is something I came up with in chat, like most of my SCP ideas. I don't know what exactly was going on that sparked it, but later on in the writing process, I realized that I was being influenced largely by Super Hexagon. For the unfamiliar, it's like a rhythm game in structure - you move according to shapes that come at you in time with the music - but the actual gameplay is closer to Super Meat Boy; you die and restart repeatedly until pattern recognition takes over and you start reacting to events in the game before they register with you. Zen-like focus.</p>
<p>I keep coming up with extra bits of story for these guys that I'm not going to clutter up the actual article with, so I'm going to post them here:</p>
<ul>
<li>Innovationism is a relatively small and newly-formed sect of the COTBG, created as a reaction to the changing relationship between humanity and machines. While it's not much now, it grows in relevance and popularity as topics like transhumanism reach the forefront of societal discussion, and it becomes the religion followed by the U.S. President in 2040, W. W. Solenoid, as mentioned in SCP-2005.</li>
<li>This particular church father claims to be a former missionary who emigrated from China due to religious persecution. In fact, he escaped due to a situation regarding his work with the Chaos Insurgency, whose progressive attitude about human augmentation has led to cooperation with members of the Church, as well as the Chinese government, who <a href="/scp-326">has dabbled with this sort of thing before</a>.</li>
<li>In case you didn't notice, the &quot;liquid feed&quot; 2360 uses isn't arbitrary in composition. Look it up.</li>
<li>The electronic components of 2360 run on a proprietary COTBG operating system named Apotheo-Sys.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>EDIT: Thanks to PeppersGhost for coming up with the mainlist name.</p>

